   "year": 6
  },
  {
   "eid": "e002258",
   "kind": "say",
   "text": "Eron, the pile went dry before I could reach it \u2014 I'm sitting on four food and you've got nine, which means this year you're the one who looks worth watching. Don't let anyone see you spending freely, and if Mako starts talking to you, you come find me before you answer him.",
   "who": "Nessa",
   "year": 6
  },
  {
   "eid": "e002259",
   "kind": "say",
   "text": "Nine doesn't make me safe, it makes me a target \u2014 I've been watching Mako all year and he's already got six, which means if he decides to move on someone he's got the strength for it and half an excuse. You're right that I'll come to you first, but Nessa, I need you to tell me straight: is Bram watching my count, because if he sees me sitting heavy while you're at four, he might think I'm hoarding from his daughter and that's a different kind of trouble.",
   "who": "Eron",
   "year": 6
  }
 ],
 "memory_summary": "",
 "memory_tokens": 19355,
 "mother_note": "Your blood is Bram's and mine \u2014 remember that means Eron is your brother, and you owe him before anyone else in this village. Trust Roan because he stood for Eron before it cost him nothing, and trust Kael and Esa because they said hard things out loud when silence would have been easier. Fear Mako most: a man who says nothing for four years and then finds the exact right moment to speak has been counting longer than you've been alive. Your father kept his word to me twice over, but he is a man who thinks in decades and measures everyone as either useful or in the way \u2014 love him, and never forget that distinction.",
